      "storyRevision": 1,
      "section": "hotels",
      "rank": 100,
      "title": "Hyatt and Brigade Group plan two Hyatt Regency hotels in Bengaluru, 600 rooms total",
      "summary": "Hyatt and Brigade Group have announced plans for two Hyatt Regency hotels in Bengaluru, together offering 600 rooms. Both properties are to be part of large-scale mixed-use developments in the city. The announcement sets out the brands and combined room count; no individual locations, opening dates or investment terms were included.",
      "verification": "officially_confirmed",
      "sourcePublishedAt": "2026-10-26T07:22:00.000Z",
      "effectiveAt": null,
      "sources": [
        {
          "publisher": "Hyatt",
          "url": "https://newsroom.hyatt.com/Hyatt_and_Brigade_Group_Announce_Plans_for_Two_New_Hyatt_Regency_Hotels_in_Bengaluru",
          "sourceType": "official",
          "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T07:22:00.000Z",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-26T14:01:55.674Z"
        }
      ],
      "terms": null,
      "expiresAt": null,
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-10-26T14:03:09.458Z",
      "changedAt": "2026-10-26T14:03:09.458Z",
      "sourceRunId": "b599ddd6-a1a6-4e59-aacd-6805f17dda6a",
      "changeType": "new",
      "active": true,
      "paragraphs": [
        "The two hotels will carry the Hyatt Regency brand and are planned within larger mixed-use projects rather than as standalone sites, according to the companies' announcement. Combined, the pair is expected to add 600 rooms to Hyatt's Bengaluru footprint.",
        "Hyatt's development pipeline in India is being expanded through partnerships with local developers, and Brigade Group is the named partner for these two Bengaluru projects. Timing for construction or opening was not disclosed."
      ],
      "keyPoints": [
        "Two Hyatt Regency hotels planned for Bengaluru under a Hyatt and Brigade Group agreement",
        "600 rooms combined across the two properties",
        "Both hotels are planned as part of large-scale mixed-use developments"
      ]
    },
    {
